# Paths the agent never needs to read. Syntax follows .gitignore.
#
# Cursor already skips everything in .gitignore. Some of those paths are
# repeated here because the hook reads only this file.
#
# .cursor/hooks/guard-test-writes.py reads this file and denies a shell
# command that names one of the paths below as a file to read (cat, grep,
# sed, and so on). Lines starting with `#` or `!` are skipped by that hook,
# so negation patterns have no effect there.
#
# test-results/ is deliberately absent: the qa-heal skill reads
# error-context.md from it.
#
# A line that starts with a slash matches in the project root only. dist/,
# build/, out/, and coverage/ start with one, because a folder of that name
# deeper down, such as app/build/ or src/dist/, is application source that the
# agent must be able to read. Change a line if your build writes elsewhere.

# Lockfiles: large, generated, and never needed to write a test.
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
bun.lock
bun.lockb

# Build output and framework caches.
node_modules/
.next/
/dist/
/build/
/out/
.turbo/
.vercel/

# Test reports and tool state. Read the test source instead.
/coverage/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.vitest/
.playwright/

# Page snapshots and console logs that playwright-cli saves.
.playwright-cli/

# Maestro debug output. It lands here when a person passes --debug-output=.
# A device log can be about 300 KB per flow.
.maestro/tests/
